        <headline>Frost Advisory issued September 25 at 3:20AM EDT until September 25 at 9:00AM EDT by NWS Charleston WV</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Temperatures as low as 33 will result in frost formation.

* WHERE...Northwest Pocahontas, Southeast Pocahontas, and Southeast
Randolph Counties.

* WHEN...Until 9 AM EDT this morning.

* IMPACTS...Frost could harm sensitive outdoor vegetation. Sensitive
outdoor plants may be killed if left uncovered.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Frost will be most prevalent across the
typical mountain valley cold spots, and in areas that do not
experience fog.
</description>
        <instruction>Take steps now to protect tender plants from the cold.

Additional information can be found at https://www.weather.gov/rlx as
well as on our X and Facebook pages.</instruction>
